    </div>

    <h2>Why SEO Pricing Varies Between Businesses</h2>

    <p>There is no single price for SEO because no two businesses face the same competitive landscape. A Jewellery Quarter independent retailer targeting "bespoke engagement rings Birmingham" operates in a fundamentally different search environment to a Colmore Row law firm competing for "commercial solicitors West Midlands." The pricing reflects this reality.</p>

    <p>Three factors determine where your business sits on the pricing spectrum:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Business size and website complexity.</strong> A 20-page brochure site requires less technical oversight than a 5,000-page e-commerce catalogue. Larger sites demand more crawl management, internal linking architecture, and content governance.</li>
      <li><strong>Keyword competition.</strong> Local service terms like "plumber Solihull" are less contested than commercial terms like "business insurance Birmingham." Higher competition means more content production, stronger link building, and longer timelines.</li>
      <li><strong>Industry regulation and trust signals.</strong> YMYL sectors (finance, health, legal) require demonstrable expertise, authoritative backlinks, and content reviewed by qualified professionals. This increases the cost of content production compared to less regulated industries.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>A transparent SEO consultant will explain exactly which of these factors apply to your business and why your quote sits where it does. If a provider cannot justify their pricing with specifics, that is a red flag.</p>

    <h2>Birmingham vs London SEO Pricing Comparison</h2>

